--------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Disassembly source (disasm/raw/*, disasm/src/*)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The files under disasm/raw/ and disasm/src/ are **derivative works**
of the original Super Robin Hood ROM. The underlying 6502 machine
code is © 1990 Codemasters Software Company Ltd. / Camerica Inc. and
its original authors. No license has been granted for this code.

The reverse-engineering annotations layered on top (labels, comments,
section banners, EQU aliases, ca65 reformatting) are © 2026 Mikolaj
and are offered under the MIT License above, but that license CANNOT
grant rights to the underlying copyrighted code.

Treat these files the same way you would treat any reverse-engineered
disassembly: for study, documentation, and interoperability purposes
only. Redistribution of the assembled ROM or of substantial verbatim
portions of it requires permission from the copyright holders.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Original game source (original_source/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The directory original_source/ is a verbatim copy of the files
published by the Oliver Twins alongside the article "Squeezing the
NES" (pages 30-35) in Wireframe Magazine issue #34, in the repo:

    https://github.com/Wireframe-Magazine/Wireframe-34
    path: super-robin-hood-nes-source-code/

That repository ships under the **Creative Commons Attribution-
NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported** license (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/legalcode

Under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 you may:
  - Share and adapt the files in original_source/
  - For non-commercial purposes only
  - With attribution to the original authors
  - Distributing any derivative work under the same license

Authorship:
  - Game code     : Philip Oliver & Andrew Oliver ("The Oliver Twins")
  - Music engine  : Gavin Raeburn ("Mega Music Driver" / MUSICED
                    lineage), bundled inside the .MUS / .PDS files
  - Publisher     : Codemasters Software Company Ltd. (UK) /
                    Camerica Inc. (North America), © 1990
  - PP1PACK.EXE   : Codemasters (original MS-DOS tile compressor),
                    published together with the source

Any redistribution of original_source/ must retain this attribution
and remain under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
4. ROM files (roms/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

  - roms/released.nes    — NOT included in this repository. The user
                           must supply their own dump of a Super
                           Robin Hood (Camerica, 1990) cartridge.
                           Copyright © 1990 Codemasters / Camerica.

  - roms/prerelease.nes  — INCLUDED. Derived from the PDS bank files
                           (ROBINV7.BC / BD / BE / BF) published in
                           original_source/ (see §3). As a derivative
                           of CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 material, this ROM is
                           itself distributed under CC BY-NC-SA 3.0:
                           non-commercial use only, attribution to
                           the Oliver Twins, and any further
                           distribution must remain under the same
                           license.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Third-party code in web / Rust dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The tools vendor or depend on open-source third-party packages
(image, ratatui, React, Vite, nginx, etc.). Each retains its own
license as declared in its package metadata (Cargo.toml, package.json,
LICENSE files inside node_modules, etc.). None of them are affected
by this file.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Summary
--------------------------------------------------------------------

If you want to reuse part of this repository:

  - Rust / TypeScript tools, build system, docs, RE annotations
      → MIT, go ahead. Attribution appreciated.

  - Disassembled game code (disasm/raw, disasm/src)
      → Not ours to license. Study / modify locally, but do not
        redistribute the reassembled ROM.

  - original_source/ and roms/prerelease.nes
      → CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (attribution: Philip & Andrew Oliver, via
        Wireframe Magazine #34). Non-commercial use only; share
        adaptations under the same license.

  - roms/released.nes
      → Not in this repository. Do not redistribute.

If you are a copyright holder and have concerns about anything in
this repository, please open an issue and we will address it.
